for a mobile user experience?” LO2: Apply Mobile-First Design Strategies Trainer’s Activities Explain the mobile-first design approach and its advantages. Show examples of layouts starting with small screens and scaling up to larger screens. Learners’ Activities Practice writing simple CSS using mobile-first media queries . Modify a basic webpage template to adapt first to mobile screens, then tablets/desktops. Share and discuss challenges in pairs. LO3: Use CSS Frameworks (Bootstrap Grid System) Trainer’s Activities Explain what CSS frameworks are and why they are useful. Demonstrate Bootstrap grid system : containers, rows, and columns. Show live examples of structuring a responsive page using Bootstrap.', 'Learners’ Activities Code along with the trainer using Bootstrap grid system . Create a responsive page layout with containers, rows, and columns. Test the layout on different screen sizes to observe responsiveness. LO4: Implement Bootstrap Components Trainer’s Activities Demonstrate key Bootstrap components : Jumbotron, Tabs, and Carousel. Show how to integrate these components into a responsive webpage. Provide a template for learners to experiment with. Learners’ Activities Add Jumbotron, Tabs, and Carousel to the template. Customize content and style, then test functionality across devices. Discuss in pairs how these components improve user interface and experience.', 'PPT Presentation, white board, marker pens and projector. Projector Laptops Projector Laptops Projector Laptops Figma / Adobe XD (optional)', '25 minutes 25 minutes 30 minutes 35 minutes', default, default, default, 'Full zipped working codes', default, default, default, default)","sqlMessage":"Field 'user_id' doesn't have a default value","sqlState":"HY000","stack":"Error: Field 'user_id' doesn't have a default value\n    at PromisePool.query (/Users/m2pro/dev/projects/nga_central_mis/backend/node_modules/mysql2/lib/promise/pool.js:36:22)\n    at MySql2PreparedQuery.execute (/Users/m2pro/dev